2026-09-28 follow-up, still isolated while PID 80898 runs:
The first candidate also accepted a zero-byte object with exit 0. A new failing
test reproduces that false success. The updated candidate requires nonempty
objects both for new verdicts and cache reuse. All 53 survey-cache tests and
Ruff pass. Three additional actual sealed-container controls assemble normally,
then deliberately truncate only the isolated a.o before returning zero:
  live implementation: assembled with the SHA256 of empty bytes (RED)
  updated candidate: assembler-refused, assemblerExitCode 0
  updated candidate without truncation: assembled, assemblerExitCode 0
The candidate cache control also refuses an empty file even when its empty-file
hash matches a cache entry. Original exit-17 evidence above remains historical;
the tracked pending patch now includes both repairs, and git apply --check passes.
No live production-script change or T05i closure is claimed.

